# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Aveline gains +1/+1 counters equal to combat damage dealt to a player by a controlled deathtouch creature.
# Forcing: Aveline is the only attacker and the opponent has no blocker, so exactly three combat damage reaches the player.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no permanents or decisions, so the combat-damage trigger resolves deterministically.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Aveline deals three damage and becomes 6/6 after its trigger resolves.
#   LOSE = Damage, the trigger, or the counter placement does not occur.
#   TIMEOUT = Combat or the triggered stack lifecycle fails to converge.
# Card roles:
#   Aveline de Grandpré — attacker, deathtouch source, trigger source, and counter recipient.
# Protocol path: Attacker declaration, combat damage, triggered stack lifecycle, counter annotations, and refreshed characteristics.

[metadata]
